          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तय करना — tay karnā — \"to fix (a date), to decide\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सभा ने अगली बैठक की तारीख़ तय की। sabhā ne aglī baiṭhak kī tārīkh tay kī. The meeting settled the date of the next one."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with ने (he or she …): उसने दिन तय किया, usne din tay kiyā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तय करना (tay karnā) joins तय to करना, \"to do\". तय is usually traced to Arabic ṭayy, \"folding up\", which reached Hindi through Persian. The sense of settling a matter is a Persian and Hindi one."
            }
          ]
        },
